<TeXmacs|2.1.4>

<style|<tuple|tmdoc|english>>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|GNU <TeXmacs> tutorial>

  This tutorial takes you, step by step, from the first start of <TeXmacs>
  to the writing of your own macros. Each chapter is short and is meant to
  be read with <TeXmacs> open next to it, so that you can try out every
  example yourself. The documents written along the way are also available
  in the <verbatim|examples> folder of this tutorial.

  <\traverse>
    <branch|A first meeting with <TeXmacs>|start/tut-start.en.tm>

    <branch|Typing your first text|text/tut-simple-text.en.tm>

    <branch|Typing mathematical formulas|math/tut-math.en.tm>

    <branch|Structured text|structure/tut-structure.en.tm>

    <branch|Writing your own macros|macros/tut-macros.en.tm>
  </traverse>

